{
  "opening": "This release introduces significant enhancements to datetime parsing capabilities, including support for C standard format codes and flexible timezone handling. It also expands the Parser class with new properties and improves robustness for various edge cases in field names and decimal formatting.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m18",
      "text": "The `Parser` class must successfully parse datetimes using C standard format codes, such as `%z` and `%j`, handling single-digit days and months correctly. The public functions `date_convert`, `extract_format`, `get_regex_for_datetime_format`, and `strf_date_convert` must be available and functional, with `dt_format_to_regex` exposed if it fits the naming convention."
    },
    {
      "id": "m20",
      "text": "The exceptions `FixedTzOffset` and `RepeatedNameError` must be accessible at the module level alongside `Parser`, `date_convert`, and `extract_format`. These names must remain stable and exported for direct import or use."
    },
    {
      "id": "m22",
      "text": "The `Parser` class must expose a `format` property that returns the original format string used to create the parser instance. The existing `parse` method must continue to function as documented without regression."
    },
    {
      "id": "m24",
      "text": "Datetime parsing must support fractional seconds with varying numbers of digits after the comma in the `%f` format specifier. This change should not alter the public API surface but must ensure correct parsing behavior for these inputs."
    },
    {
      "id": "m26",
      "text": "The `Parser` class and `extract_format` function must allow hyphens within field names in the format specification. This ensures that patterns containing hyphenated identifiers are parsed correctly without raising errors."
    },
    {
      "id": "m33",
      "text": "Decimal format strings must support grouping characters, specifically commas and underscores, within the number representation. The `Parser` class and `extract_format` function must handle these characters correctly during parsing operations."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please verify that all listed public names are correctly exported and that the new datetime and formatting features work as described across different Python versions."
}
